30:57.500 --> 30:58.340
It feels like a paradox.

30:58.760 --> 31:03.500
But this raises a crucial point about how complex distributed networks actually behave

31:03.500 --> 31:04.800
in mathematical space.

31:04.960 --> 31:05.240
How so?

31:05.380 --> 31:11.660
When a surgeon inserts that DBS electrode, they are not targeting a bad node to turn it off.

31:12.060 --> 31:14.720
They are targeting the boundary of the entire manifold.

31:15.240 --> 31:16.200
I'm not sure I'm following.

31:16.540 --> 31:18.740
How does hitting one point change the whole manifold?

31:19.080 --> 31:20.240
Let's work through an analogy.

31:20.240 --> 31:26.940
Think of the distributed pausal manifold, that pathological state causing the tremor like

31:26.940 --> 31:30.300
an incredibly massive heavy vault door in a bank.

31:30.540 --> 31:30.560
Okay.

31:30.640 --> 31:31.880
A huge steel door.

31:32.000 --> 31:33.760
The entire door represents the problem.

31:33.920 --> 31:34.100
Yeah.

31:34.180 --> 31:37.780
It is all connected, all one solid piece of steel.

