It's too heavy.

31:44.640 --> 31:44.880
Right.

31:44.880 --> 31:46.820
The inertia of the whole system is too great.

31:47.080 --> 31:52.960
But if you find the exact hinge of that door, you can swing the entire massive structure

31:52.960 --> 31:54.580
with just a gentle push of your hand.

31:54.680 --> 31:55.080
Oh, wow.

31:55.620 --> 31:56.300
I see it now.

31:56.360 --> 31:56.560
Right.

31:57.020 --> 31:59.180
Deep brain stimulation is finding the hinge.

31:59.580 --> 32:03.160
The specific spot in the basal ganglia isn't where the tremor lives.

32:03.520 --> 32:06.780
It is simply the topological hinge of the entire brain network.

32:06.920 --> 32:07.460
That's brilliant.

32:07.680 --> 32:12.360
The high frequency electrical pulse delivered by the wire doesn't suppress a local BAD signal.

32:12.360 --> 32:18.400
It acts as a physical force that kicks the entire global brain network out of the symptom-causing

32:18.400 --> 32:22.840
geometry and forces it to swing into a new, healthy geometry.

32:23.060 --> 32:28.140
You are changing the topology of the whole system by pushing firmly on its boundary constraint.

32:28.220 --> 32:28.700
Exactly.

32:29.120 --> 32:31.280
The hinge that moves the heaviest door.

