38:09.200 --> 38:10.420
The material is the math.

38:10.420 --> 38:13.400
That is a beautiful and highly accurate analogy.

38:13.880 --> 38:17.800
On the guitar, the physical constraint of the string dictates the resonant frequency.

38:18.200 --> 38:18.400
Exactly.

38:18.660 --> 38:24.300
And what is truly fascinating is that this exact realization that imposing structural constraints

38:24.300 --> 38:30.580
on a system dictates a vastly superior output compared to just crunching raw data is causing

38:30.580 --> 38:34.820
a massive, quiet revolution right now in the field of artificial intelligence.

38:35.040 --> 38:40.800
Which perfectly transitions us into Section 6 of the paper, AI and the Return of Structure.

38:40.980 --> 38:41.200
Right.

38:41.860 --> 38:47.700
In this section, Flyxion explores the CLIO framework, which stands for Constraint Leverage

38:47.700 --> 38:49.220
Inference and Optimization.

38:49.680 --> 38:53.800
This section is a direct critique of the current zeitgeist in Silicon Valley, actually.

38:54.480 --> 38:58.380
Flyxion reviews three recent cutting-edge AI papers to make this point.

38:58.480 --> 38:59.300
Okay, let's go through them.

38:59.300 --> 39:04.560
There's Wu and Zhang's work on graph neural networks for analyzing medical pathology,

39:05.140 --> 39:11.640
Taya Azal's research on MNREC news classification, and Maras et al.'s study on a dual-explanation

39:11.640 --> 39:16.360
AI for diagnosing basal cell carcinoma, which is a type of skin cancer.

39:16.520 --> 39:22.300
And while these papers deal with entirely different types of data, microscopic tissue, African languages,

39:22.500 --> 39:27.080
and skin lesions, they all point to the exact same glaring limitation in modern tech.

39:27.280 --> 39:27.720
Yes.

39:27.720 --> 39:30.920
The failure of what Flyxion calls pure statistics.

39:31.260 --> 39:31.520
Yes.

39:32.060 --> 39:36.080
Modern AI, particularly the massive large language models we interact with daily,

39:36.460 --> 39:38.720
largely operates on a philosophy of brute force.

39:38.780 --> 39:40.020
Just throwing computer the problem.

39:40.340 --> 39:40.780
Exactly.

39:41.220 --> 39:42.780
The prevailing wisdom has been,

39:43.660 --> 39:47.900
throw billions or trillions of unstructured data points at a massive neural network,

39:48.320 --> 39:50.360
give it endless computational power,

39:50.700 --> 39:53.940
and let it try to learn everything about the universe from scratch,

39:53.940 --> 39:56.840
purely by crunching statistical probabilities.

39:57.160 --> 39:57.360
Right.

39:57.480 --> 39:59.580
The AI doesn't actually know what a dog is.

39:59.680 --> 40:05.400
It just knows that the word dog statistically appears near the word bark 87% of the time.

40:05.460 --> 40:06.580
It's just pattern matching.

40:06.800 --> 40:10.900
It is predicting the next word based on pure, unconstrained math.

40:10.900 --> 40:13.280
But that brute force approach is hitting a wall.

40:13.820 --> 40:16.420
Pure statistics suffer from the curse of dimensionality.

40:16.800 --> 40:21.380
The search space of possible answers is essentially infinite, and it's filled with noise.

40:21.500 --> 40:22.120
So it gets confused.

40:22.340 --> 40:24.980
Let's look deeply at Wu and Zhang's pathology AI.

40:25.480 --> 40:31.140
They were trying to get an AI to look at highly complex images of human tissue samples and diagnosed diseases.

40:31.140 --> 40:40.460
When they just fed the AI raw pixel-by-pixel image data and let it run pure statistical analysis the way a standard image recognition AI works,

40:40.820 --> 40:41.320
it struggled.

40:41.900 --> 40:46.860
It got confused by visual noise, staining differences, or slight variations in tissue prep.

40:47.100 --> 40:54.660
Because to a purely statistical AI, a pixel of a cancer cell and a pixel of a healthy cell are just numbers.

40:54.960 --> 40:55.420
Exactly.

40:55.580 --> 40:56.820
They have no intrinsic meaning.

40:57.520 --> 41:00.560
But then Wu and Zhang changed their approach.

41:00.560 --> 41:07.880
They used a graph neural network, and crucially, they embedded what they called a pathological admissibility prior.

41:08.120 --> 41:09.440
Okay, let's break that phrase down.

41:10.060 --> 41:11.860
Pathological admissibility prior.

41:12.400 --> 41:14.680
What exactly did they do to the AI?

41:15.180 --> 41:25.140
Instead of letting the AI look at independent pixels, they mathematically taught the AI the spatial geometry of how human tissues are structurally supposed to relate to each other.

41:25.220 --> 41:26.120
Oh, they gave it rules.

41:26.260 --> 41:27.500
They gave it structural boundaries.

41:27.500 --> 41:36.640
A graph neural network uses nodes and edges, so they define the nodes as specific types of cells, and the edges as physical proximity or chemical interaction.

41:36.760 --> 41:37.700
So they taught it in anatomy.

41:37.960 --> 41:41.640
They essentially said to the AI, you don't need to learn human anatomy from scratch.

41:41.760 --> 41:42.440
Here are the rules.

41:42.860 --> 41:46.460
Epithelial cells form continuous sheets in this specific shape.

41:47.100 --> 41:50.000
Glands are hollow tubes surrounded by these specific cells.

41:50.380 --> 41:52.440
Cells cannot physically overlap in space.

41:52.480 --> 41:54.640
They gave the AI the constraints of human anatomy.

41:54.640 --> 41:55.640
Precisely.

41:56.140 --> 41:59.680
They didn't tell the AI how to explicitly diagnose the cancer.

42:00.140 --> 42:06.780
They just confined its mathematical reasoning to the admissibility manifold of actual biological tissue.

42:07.100 --> 42:07.620
That might happen.

42:07.860 --> 42:16.360
The moment they introduced that geometric structure, the AI completely crushed the purely statistical models in diagnostic performance.

42:16.360 --> 42:18.820
It's the highway traffic analogy coming back.

42:19.400 --> 42:28.240
Instead of letting the AI look at a million random cars to try and figure out the concept of a commute, they just showed it the shape of the highway and said, the cars have to stay between these lines.

42:28.500 --> 42:29.860
It's exactly the same principle.

42:30.120 --> 42:34.080
The constraints eliminated all the impossible mathematical guesses instantly.

42:34.080 --> 42:35.600
That is exactly what happened.

42:35.760 --> 42:41.280
And we see the exact same principle applied to language in Tay's paper on classifying news articles in Amharic.

42:41.460 --> 42:43.020
Amharic is an Ethiopian language.

42:43.080 --> 42:43.320
Yes.

42:43.640 --> 42:47.060
Amharic is a complex, morphologically rich language.

42:47.700 --> 42:52.720
A purely statistical AI straws with it because words change their shape based on context.

42:52.840 --> 42:53.540
It's hard to predict.

42:54.120 --> 42:54.360
Very.

42:54.960 --> 42:59.840
Tay's team didn't try to improve the AI by giving it more raw text data to crunch.

43:00.260 --> 43:02.060
Instead, they gave it an ontology.

43:02.060 --> 43:07.180
Explain what an ontology is in computational terms because that sounds like a philosophy word.

43:07.540 --> 43:10.520
In philosophy, ontology is the study of what exists.

43:11.180 --> 43:14.380
In computer science, an ontology is a semantic geometry.

43:14.760 --> 43:15.800
A semantic geometry.

43:15.880 --> 43:21.320
It is a rigid mathematical map of how words, concepts, and categories relate to each other structurally.

43:21.660 --> 43:23.400
It defines hierarchies.

43:23.520 --> 43:24.120
Give me an example.

43:24.540 --> 43:30.780
For example, an ontology explicitly defines that Addis Ababa is the capital of Ethiopia, which is a country in Africa.

43:30.780 --> 43:34.280
It creates a web of rigid semantic constraints.

43:34.640 --> 43:36.860
So it maps the meaning, not just the letters.

43:37.140 --> 43:37.340
Right.

43:37.720 --> 43:53.800
Once the AI was forced to map its statistical guesses onto the structured ontology, once its reasoning was confined inside a semantic admissibility, manifold its accuracy in classifying complex news topics skyrocketed, the structure eliminated the noise.

43:53.800 --> 44:01.600
And this concept of constraining the AI's reasoning brings us to the modest skin cancer paper, which I found deeply reassuring from a medical standpoint.

44:01.680 --> 44:02.780
It's very promising work.

44:02.880 --> 44:05.840
They focus on something called explanation as a trajectory constraint.

44:06.200 --> 44:09.680
This is a critical breakthrough for trust in medical AI.

44:09.680 --> 44:16.980
Usually, when a standard AI diagnoses a skin mole as cancer from a photo, it operates as a black box.

44:17.180 --> 44:18.760
It makes a statistical guess.

44:19.040 --> 44:20.340
We don't know how it got there.

44:20.460 --> 44:20.700
Right.

44:20.960 --> 44:24.340
If a doctor asks the AI, why do you think this is cancer?

