A separate, secondary subsystem tries to invent a post hoc reason to justify the guess.

44:32.120 --> 44:33.040
It makes up an excuse.

44:33.040 --> 44:33.560
Exactly.

44:34.040 --> 44:39.720
It points to a blurry patch of pixels and essentially hallucinates a plausible-sounding medical reason.

44:39.980 --> 44:42.000
It is making up a story after the fact.

44:42.100 --> 44:45.100
Which is terrifying if you are the patient relying on that diagnosis.

44:45.140 --> 44:46.020
Absolutely terrifying.

44:46.400 --> 44:50.280
But Mata's prove that you can fundamentally alter how the AI thinks.

44:50.760 --> 44:55.940
By using a dual-explanation architecture, they constrained the AI's actual inference trajectory.

44:56.200 --> 44:57.680
They put guardrails on its logic.

44:57.680 --> 45:04.760
They forced the neural network to only operate within an admissibility manifold defined by clinically recognized medical features.

45:05.000 --> 45:09.860
Meaning the AI is physically, mathematically not allowed to make a jump in logic,

45:10.320 --> 45:18.400
unless that jump maps directly to a real medical concept like a regular border or color asymmetry that a human dermatologist would use.

45:18.400 --> 45:28.180
Exactly. It cannot hallucinate a reason based on random statistical noise because the constraints of the system forbid it from entering that mathematical space.

45:28.300 --> 45:28.900
It's blocked.

45:29.240 --> 45:34.820
The constraint forces the AI to be inherently explainable by its very design, not as an afterthought.

45:35.420 --> 45:39.840
Its reasoning process is identical to the geometry of human clinical reasoning.

45:40.000 --> 45:43.240
This raises a massive question about the future of technology.

45:43.340 --> 45:43.860
Let's hear it.

45:43.860 --> 45:49.200
Are we saying that the current trend in Silicon Valley, just building bigger and bigger data centers,

45:49.600 --> 45:58.180
throwing exponentially more raw data and brute compute power at these massive LLMs, is fundamentally a dead end?

45:58.300 --> 45:59.960
That's the billion-dollar question.

46:00.080 --> 46:05.840
Do we have to abandon pure statistics and start giving AI these structural boundaries, these constraint manifolds,

46:05.980 --> 46:09.520
if we want to achieve true, reliable artificial intelligence?

46:09.520 --> 46:15.260
Flyxion strongly argues yes, and the empirical data from these papers unequivocally backs it up.

46:15.560 --> 46:21.660
Pure statistics eventually plateau because you can never have enough data to cover every possible permutation of the universe.

46:21.680 --> 46:23.080
The noise just takes over.

46:23.400 --> 46:25.980
And the noise eventually drowns out the signal.

46:26.800 --> 46:30.340
Section 16.4 of the paper calls this the return of structure.

46:30.480 --> 46:31.440
The return of structure.

46:31.440 --> 46:36.940
It suggests that true intelligence isn't about having access to an infinite database of answers.

46:37.460 --> 46:43.620
It is about having the precise structural constraints needed to instantly eliminate all the wrong answers.

46:43.880 --> 46:47.260
Intelligence is a process of elimination guided by geometry.

46:47.600 --> 46:49.020
That's a great way to summarize it.

46:49.220 --> 46:53.840
It blows my mind how this admissibility principle applies to literally everything we've talked about.

46:53.840 --> 46:59.020
Proteins folding into cages, biological brains surfing the edge of chaos,

